A||||4||My7Fieros||Cannister purge........on a V6?...||||8||
Z||000000||My7Fieros||07-23-2000||11:01 PM||||Im having a high idle prob. on my 87 GT. Typically this is an easy problem, but Im comming close to wits end on this one. It idles around 1500-1600 RPM in park/neutral. In gear, it idles around 900-1000 (about average). The EGR tube is fine, and I have searched high and low for a vacuum leak...cannot find one (or even hear one) at all. The timing is set correct Im sure. <BR>Now, I am getting the "idle air control" flashes on my idiot light. I have yet to replace it with a new one, but have checked with two other known good ones from two of my other Fieros...no change. Ive got the 1987 Service manual (the great big phone book size one, the Fiero Bible, if you will)and it goes through all sorts of scenerios for this problem. According to the book, my IAC is fine (which I suspected anyway). Ive already checked the cruise control, and the air conditioning (yes, it can cause a high idle)...just about the only thing left is something about a cannister purge, but it only mentions the 4banger engines.....is there such an animal on the V6? and if so, could this be my prob? HELP!!!!!!!!!! TIA, Brian||||reg||8
Z||000001||terryk||07-24-2000||01:08 AM||||Get a can of carb cleaner and start spray around the intake. I suspect you have a vacuum leak somewhere. EGR tube, EGR mount, one of the vacuum lines, booster leaking, etc.<P>You'll know when you spray the leaking area.||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||07-24-2000||03:33 AM||||OK Duh, I believe I found the can purge..could it be that large black can next to my air filter? DUH! anyway, I changed the map sensor (Im grabbing at straws now) and it helped considerbly. But its still idleing at around 1200; just enought to set a code...AAAAARRRGGGGG!!!!!!!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><BR>Ill give the carb thing a try terry, thanx<P>Click, BANG!!!! &lt;---pulling out my service weapon and shooting the car!!!!!<BR>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 07-24-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 07-24-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||bcibob670||07-24-2000||07:05 AM||||brian ...<P>believe me   I feel your pain ..(to quote the pres.)   have you tried diddling with the electrical harness while the engine is running?   on my four banger I have an idle adj stop on the throttle body . ...also the carb cleaner trick is great i used it on my grand am.   <P>Stay safe <BR>and remember your best weapon is between your ears...( to quote my academy instructor of 10 years ago)   <P>bob   <BR>brockton massachusetts.  ||||reg||6
Z||000004||Carrolles||07-24-2000||07:23 AM||||Brian,<P>Have you looked inside the throttle body to see if the butterfly is being kept from shutting completely by a buildup of carbon deposits?  Mine was.  I used Ed Park's de-carbonizing kit and everything sure cleared up afterwards.<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
